{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "model": "SidecarBoundary",
  "assumptions": [
    "Each physical undo effect follows the slot, byte, page-lifetime, and committed-insert obligations checked by SidecarUndo under its declared policy and bounds. Loser-before-deleted-image undo is assumed, not proved here.",
    "The history instance reuses the actual history WAL and operators. Unused state is substituted with constants, and scan is mapped to completed discovery. This is predicate reuse, not action refinement.",
    "Event discovery is complete at durable commit and there is one registered replica. The detailed history model separately checks delayed discovery and retention.",
    "The WAL sequence remains as an oracle after archive deletion. Actual fragment reads require retained records. Durable transaction and replica progress remain known independently of removed archive records.",
    "A pre-commit source crash aborts the transaction. A durable commit is redone. Recovery replays the surviving WAL and rebuilds protection before reopening garbage collection and archive deletion.",
    "The single writer holds the parent lock until commit or abort. The model excludes own reads during partial undo and does not prove MVCC family identity or engine conformance.",
    "There is one retained old snapshot and a savepoint after operation 1. Operation 2 is cancelled. Each new value has two abstract chunks and each image has 2 * Parts fragments.",
    "The first fragment append and acquisition of its construction pin are one atomic event.",
    "The replica stages every surviving operation in the source transaction and commits the full batch plus progress atomically. This model does not represent non-Sidecar table mutations or actual replica isolation."
  ],
